      "narrative": "The most telling hiring signal this week is not any single appointment but the combination. Amir Bar — an assistant professor at Imperial College London and a former Meta researcher — brings serious computer vision and multimodal credentials to AMI's London footprint. Ayaan Naveed Malik, a recent Stanford graduate joining in New York, arrives with a background in robotics and multimodal AI, exactly the domains where JEPA-style world models need to prove themselves. Together they suggest AMI is assembling the technical bench to move from theory to working systems.\n\nThe third hire is Haoyi Li, who is joining in Singapore. He is not a machine-learning researcher, but rather a large-scale developer infrastructure engineer known for work at Databricks and Dropbox, and the author of the Mill build tool. His GitHub activity this week — closing issues in his own `com-lihaoyi/mill` repo and commenting on a Scala 3 pull request — confirms he is already active on infrastructure concerns. Hiring someone of Li's profile at this stage signals that AMI is taking the underlying engineering platform seriously, not just the research layer above it.",
